WEBVTT

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.610
They're here?

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.920
On this terrain, they won't be able to run anywhere.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.590
The loot'll be ours if we drive them into a corner.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:20.200
Our tires-

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:23.670
Now!

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.600
Fire away!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.340
Now, come out nice and easy.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:53.960
Shit!

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.830
Is the cargo a goner, too?

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:08.910
Here.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.790
Our destination is Essan.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.420
Our time limit is 48 hours.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:24.180
Your mission this time is to safely bring this case to the town without fail.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.250
Yes, sir.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:32.190
Essan's a northern town that will require the crossings of several snow-covered mountains, right?

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:36.280
Essan, Essan, the white land~

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.190
In this town that has forgotten about summer~

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:44.540
Winter comes and winter comes again~

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.200
What are you doing?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.080
Just saying what kind of a place Essan is.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.880
It's a place that transporters have a tough time getting to, indeed.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:01.510
But heck, isn't this a simple delivery job?

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.340
Why do we have to go?

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.960
In the mountain path to Essan,

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.220
we've received news there have been
mountain bandits lurking around lately.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.600
Mountain bandits?

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.490
That road is the town's only lifeline.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.700
We have received pleas to do something about it.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:24.480
And that's where we come in to deliver
the cargo and also investigate the situation.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.530
Understood.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.870
And what's this cargo?

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:34.730
To have the army involved in this must mean that it's a rather important item inside.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.750
Yes.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.490
It's...

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.350
LT...

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.270
Wait...

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.710
Please wait...

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.260
I can't take it anymore...

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.180
Dying here...

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:57.740
Cargo's too heavy...

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.290
Then stop saying useless things.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.940
The more you speak, the more stamina you lose.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.480
Sorry...

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.220
If only I could've driven past those bandits more efficiently...

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.120
I got injured, too...

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.060
Stop.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.720
Don't blame yourself so much.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:12.710
That's right.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:15.390
No one's saying it was your fault.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.400
But...

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.930
No buts, dammit.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:22.650
It's our superiors' fault for giving intelligence that underestimated them.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.740
It's coming from where we fell.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.220
They plan on coming after us.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:31.760
Let's go.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.030
We need to get this to the town of Essan by tomorrow morning.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.330
Damn it!

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.270
Damn it!

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:43.580
Hey!

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.320
Cut it out already.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:51.990
There's nothing here that's worth tons of money!

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.760
Piece of shit...

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.540
That was a total waste of our time and energy.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.820
Now, don't say that, Mueller.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.920
The hunting ain't over yet.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.590
These things ain't enough to fill our appetite at all.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:12.560
All these canned foods are supposed to be essential to these soldiers crossing the mountains,

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:16.350
but what does it tell you if they left these behind?

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:18.600
Then...

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:19.790
That's right.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.090
That means they only took the real treasure away with them.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.610
This one might be a big jackpot.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.860
Bastards!

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.480
Which way did they go?

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:29.420
Up there.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.450
But why?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:36.140
Amateurs would leave their stuff behind
and desperately climb down the mountains,

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.210
but these guys are the proud and honorable soldiers of the Empire.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.960
They only descend the mountain after they finish their mission.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.840
Or you mean, after they become corpses.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:50.180
Soldiers' thinking patterns are so simple;

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.180
they're so easy to figure out.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:56.070
They gave us a lot of shit during the war,

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.060
but those times are long gone.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.240
It's our turn this time.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:11.710
Does it hurt?

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:12.630
I'm fine.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:13.780
Really.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.430
You don't look it.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:18.000
The wounds aren't deep;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.830
it should be okay after I rest a little.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.330
Forgive me.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.290
It would help if we lit a fire,

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.200
but we can't let the bandits know we're here.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.000
Sorry.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.570
I'm burdening the entire unit.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:31.800
Don't worry about it.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.740
Just think about resting up now.

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:42.420
The distance between here and Essan is about 16 or 17 kilometers.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.370
We're off our course by a lot.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:48.280
It's only an easy hour if we had our car.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:53.490
In this snow, suppose we walk four kilometers per hour...

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.790
...we'd need at least four hours.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:59.340
But this snowstorm should end by tomorrow.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.220
If we depart at dawn,

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:03.020
we should barely make it by my calculations.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.060
Yeah.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.780
So, the main problem is those bandits.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:12.010
I'm sure they're not crazy enough to attack us in this blizzard.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:17.100
But even if we leave at sunrise,
what shall we do if they come after us then?

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.360
Sorry, it's all my fault.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:24.980
We're stuck in these mountains
with no car nor any winter combat equipment.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:28.270
We do have two rifles and ammunition.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.700
But, we can't do anything-

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.200
Now, now...

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.040
Machs!

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.490
Yes, sir!

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:38.920
Stop dwelling on things that happened already!

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:40.320
LT...

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:41.660
Listen!

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:44.550
If you consider yourself a soldier, then think about it.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:48.650
Think about what we need to do to complete our mission...

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:49.960
...and what we need to accomplish.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.390
Yes, sir...

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.350
Everyone understand?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.390
No hiding anything here.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:04.410
Yes, sir.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.140
Fair and square.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:07.900
One, two...

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.990
Hey, hey, hey...

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:14.080
Is this really all we have?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.200
Cat food?!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.420
What the hell?

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:17.610
Sorry...

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:20.400
Well, better than nothing.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.450
Then, let's split these up equally into four parts.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:25.710
Wait just a minute!

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:28.630
Aren't these items military surplus?

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:31.090
Where did you steal these from?

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.600
Ahh, well, from... you know...

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.260
Emergency provisions!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:39.320
All soldiers should be prepared and stocked for any type of situation.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:43.040
Don't preach about the way soldiers should be when you bring alcohol on missions!

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.310
Big guy, help me!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.090
Y-Yes, sir.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:50.240
Get your hands off, Corporal!

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.980
I need to bring down the hammer of justice on this traitor!

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.570
Blockheads like you-

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.770
Corporal, what are you-

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:02.740
Now, you're part of the traitors, too, 2nd Lieutenant.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.690
If all of us were to fall here,

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:10.120
what will happen to the people that are waiting for us?

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.100
The corporal's right.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.710
Never mind how they were brought onto this mission,

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:19.980
these rations will help us accomplish our military mission, no?

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.190
Let's eat.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.930
Eat and recharge ourselves.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.680
All right, then.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:30.290
Oreld.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.380
S-Sir!

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.490
Divide our remaining rations into four.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.480
Four equivalent parts.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.190
Yes, sir!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.220
This is for finishing our mission.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.160
All men, eat up everything.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.200
But...

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.410
...Oreld only gets cat food.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.420
I am friggin' freezing...

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.140
This lousy coat is just heavy;

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.370
it doesn't keep us warm at all...

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:04.470
The temperature at night around here reaches -50° Celsius apparently.

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:08.190
Lieutenant, the sergeant major is...

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.320
What a severe fever...

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.650
Hey, pull yourself together, Machs.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:17.230
What should I do?

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:18.970
How can I-

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:19.990
LT.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:23.410
Lieuteant, fire's...

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:28.560
Yes, that's like openly telling those bandits where we are located.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:29.970
That may be,

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:33.890
but these bandits know the terrain better to begin with.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:36.000
They obviously know that we're hiding here...

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:40.380
...And it'd be more natural for us to think that way.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:44.270
What's scarier right now is this freezing weather.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:47.340
If we spend the whole night without a fire,

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:51.480
not only Machs, but we're all going to freeze to death.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:53.980
Okay, then.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.910
Boss, it's them.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.910
That little hut to the north.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.620
Your thinking that they went upwards was right, boss.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:15.150
But they've climbed too much.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.490
We'll have to take a long detour to catch them.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:19.520
Shall we go after them right now?

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:22.190
Don't be in such a hurry.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:28.690
These are soldiers that were able to drag us around in this blizzard.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:31.590
They need to make us enjoy this more.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:39.120
We lit the fire, but it's not warming us up at all.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:40.950
There's no wood to burn.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.760
They're all frozen stiff even if there are any.

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:45.280
We'll be fine with this,

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.490
but Machs...

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.160
Yo, big guy.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:48.890
Yes?

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:53.660
In this situation, there are two more methods to warm our bodies up.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:58.610
One is to have everyone drink this and warm us up from the inside.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:01.960
But, isn't that bad?

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.170
The lieutenant is a minor, too.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.890
Be ashamed of yourself as a human!

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:13.220
That leaves us with the other method.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.790
No, I can't.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.380
Even though I'm your superior officer,

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:21.480
I can't let you do something so dangerous.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:24.400
I'll do anything for the lieutenant.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.240
Really?

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:30.620
Me and the lieutenant?!

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:32.020
Idiot!

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.020
All of us!

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.700
All of us, you pervert!

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.960
What the hell are you thinking at a time like this?

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.150
You're right...

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.270
But, I can't...

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:44.640
Didn't you just say you'd do anything?

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:45.940
Was that a lie?

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.300
Or a deception?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.490
But, umm...

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:50.960
The LT's life is on the line here!

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:54.890
What are you two whispering to each other about?

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.630
Umm...

00:13:58.260 --> 00:13:59.860
Go, big guy.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.610
Go die!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:02.950
L-Lieutenant!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:03.990
What is it?

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:05.250
Umm...

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:07.320
What?

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.570
Go, go!

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.780
Lieutenant, you're cold, right?

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:13.650
Huh?

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:16.880
A blizzard night like this...

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:17.580
Umm...

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.960
Sheep! Sheep!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.350
Ah, yeah.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:25.640
Have you ever seen sheep cuddle up and sleep together?

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:27.200
Sheep?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.660
No, I haven't.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.270
N-Neither have I, but...

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:37.300
...t-to overcome this coldness at night, we...

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:38.730
What?

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:41.690
Say what you want to say already!

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:44.230
Sir!

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:49.050
Lieutenant, please cuddle up and sleep with me like sheep do!

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:52.660
Corporal...

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:57.830
S-Sir...

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:27.340
How does it look?

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:28.910
We're completely surrounded.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:31.600
Can you tell how many there are?

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.560
About twenty.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:35.080
Lieutenant...

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:38.160
I'll try to buy you as much time as I can here.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:39.320
Wait.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:42.900
The rest of it goes like "Lieutenant,
you take these two with you" or something?

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:44.920
Fool.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:52.990
On the battlefield, the duty of the commander is to accomplish the mission with the least amount of casualties.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:00.990
It sounds cool to say that,

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:04.850
but how about we be a bit more realistic?

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:08.450
We still have some time before the sun rises.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:09.360
Right?

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:10.840
Oreld.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.150
You'll be sniped if you stand up like that.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.460
Besides...

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.620
Even if we hole up in here,

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:28.840
they'll just wait for us until we run out of supplies here.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.520
And how do you plan on using that wool?

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:34.270
I'm making preparations for the snow.

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:36.430
Oh, you're finally up, Machs?

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.450
Are you okay?

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:38.340
Yeah.

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:39.350
Somewhat.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:17.040
What?!

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:26.680
Impossible!

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.650
What? A sled?

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.580
Did you see the look on their faces?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:38.400
Yeah, I would've never thought of freezing a blanket using melted snow.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:40.960
Hey, if you were poor as a kid,

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.820
you develop a habit of making anything into a toy.

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:44.890
What do you think?

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:47.840
We'll be able to just make it in time like this.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:49.240
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:54.400
But I feel ashamed for being able to do nothing but show my back to the enemies...

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.100
We didn't lose.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:18:01.490
We may not have won against the bandits,

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:03.520
but we haven't lost the mission yet.

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.420
You must deliver this.

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:09.160
There's someone waiting for this over there.

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:13.150
We haven't lost... eh?

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:14.440
Okay!

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:19.300
To accomplish our mission, we'll just keep on
running and running and running until Essan!

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:20.160
Roger that!

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:24.050
He might've been an idiot,

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:25.870
but he didn't deserve to die.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.500
Who cares about the treasure anymore!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:34.500
We're not letting them get off this mountain alive!

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:40.050
They're coming after us faster than I'd expected.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.100
Control this properly!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.190
It's the enemies!

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.020
Hand over the rifles.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:05.810
I'll take them on.

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:08.250
Then that makes running all the way here pointless!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.410
He's right!

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.190
Then what do you suggest?!

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:14.460
I'll stay behind.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:15.630
What?

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:19.180
Were you not listening to what I was saying this morning?

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:20.720
This is the LT's duty.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.930
I'll... stay behind.

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.030
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:29.670
Yeah, yeah.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:30.310
Hey, wait!

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:30.420
Finish this up, big guy.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:32.020
Let me go!
Finish this up, big guy.

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:38.100
We'll fire all at once!

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.340
Aim properly!

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.040
Taking me on with one pistol?

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:48.040
Don't be joking with me!

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:54.830
He did it?

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:04.660
What are you shooting all the way there for?

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:07.090
Tighten up your marksmanship a bit!

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:13.640
Patients at Essan...

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:18.940
...are waiting for the serum we're bringing...

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:20.420
Serum...

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:22.990
That was your treasure?

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:31.210
Such an honorable mission, soldier.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.280
Corporal!

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:42.010
Make sure you deliver that serum properly!

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:45.300
Because we're all from that village!

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:58.130
Corporal...

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:00.130
He got swallowed by the avalanche...

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.480
"We haven't lost the mission" ?

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:09.780
If you die, then we lose the battle and the mission!

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:16.000
You... You... stupid corporal!

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:22.410
...stupid corporal!

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:26.880
Umm...

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:34.350
Excuse me...

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:35.620
Corporal!

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:36.640
Big guy!

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:37.940
You're alive!

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:40.790
My hand can't hold on anymore!

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.110
Please lift me up already!

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:52.830
Look.

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:54.970
It's the town of Essan.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.590
We made it somehow.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:34.360
Mer-kun, I heard that Oreld got a girlfriend!

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:37.420
I still can't believe it, but...

00:23:37.420 --> 00:23:39.240
Huh?! It's for real?!

00:23:39.820 --> 00:23:41.890
Next time, "The Woman in the Morning Mist".

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:43.920
Come get us if you're not scared!
